A||N||6||862M4inCA||Bad headlight relay or switch?||||5||
Z||000000||862M4inCA||05-02-2000||06:18 AM||||Well fortunately this is not a headlight motor related question (whew!) The other day while driving, I turned my headlights on to find that I had no dashlights or tail lights but the headlights were working. After checking things out, I discovered the fuse had blown. I replaced the fuse and it blew immediately after turning the lights back on, indicating a short somewhere. I checked several places in the circuit and didn't find anything that looked suspicious, and decided to try another fuse. Viola, I have dashlights, however now when I turn my headlights off, everything BUT the headlights go off. The only way to get the to go off is to just turn the park lights on and back off. I did notice tho that when the headlights are turned on (switch in the on position) I hear a "click" indicating a relay has become active. When I turn them off, I don't hear it click back, but I DO hear another click when the park lights are turned back on (no headlights, just the park). Would this indicate a switch problem, or relay problem? I'm not sure if it's the headlight motor relay I'm hearing or not, but it's appearing to originate on the fender next to the left headlight. Any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||chris6878||05-02-2000||12:08 PM||||I was going to post the same thing...  i just got my headlights working up and down yesterday like they should...  when i turn em off, they stay up and the head lights are still burning a little,  then turn park lights on and off again...  they go down...   what gives?   <P>||||reg||3
Z||000002||862M4inCA||05-02-2000||02:32 PM||||well mine don't just burn a little, They're completely on, I can even hit my dimmer switch and switch from hi to lo beam, and they won't go back off unless I hit the park lights, then you hear a click and the headlights go back off.||||reg||1
Z||000003||chris6878||05-02-2000||05:13 PM||||anybody?||||reg||5
Z||000004||Phil||05-02-2000||06:25 PM||||I would suspect the dash switch||||reg||1
Z||000005||sdm1964||05-02-2000||07:56 PM||||Hey mine did the same thing!!!! It is the relay on the side of the fender. Not the one on the motors.  The one all by it self. Drove me nuts. Try it, fixed mine. Its not the switch, i bought 2 thinking the same thing.the one for the headlights and the one for the motors are 2 different kinds i think, not sure on that one, I got lucky, I had just bought another fiero and the headlights worked right, motors burnt up, just started changing peices till i got it fixed, that was accuatly the first thing i replaced.<p>[This message has been edited by sdm1964 (edited 05-02-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000006||chris6878||05-02-2000||11:18 PM||||i think i am going to have to agree with sdm, went out to get in my fiero after dark this evening...  flip my headlights on, and the passenger side motor doesnt come up (its the only one working right now, my other is shot)  i pop the hood,  move that relay on the fender wall around and boom.. they go up and down again.. lol...      going to have to get a new one..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
